win32u: GetClipBox returns an all-zero box for an empty clip region (Neutron#59).

What he saw (reporter, Neutron#59): "Lightroom CC Camera Matching Profile does not stay
selected" -- "I can hover over the selection and see the change in the image but clicking it
and moving my mouse off the field causes it to revert to adobe standard." Reproduced in the lab
at the reporter's 3440x1440: Camera Matching / B&W tiles get the selection border but are not
applied; at 3840x2160 they apply.

Mechanism: on mouse-up Lightroom's Profile Browser (AgGridView, one child window per profile
group) reads the "visibleRect" of every group window: GetDC(child) + GetClipBox. When a group
window lies wholly below its toplevel (a tall group such as Camera Matching or B&W pushes the
following collapsed groups below the window), Wine returned NULLREGION with the leftover of the
failed device-rect intersection as the box, e.g. (0,0)-(0,-26). Lightroom turns that inverted
rect into an invalid range and the click handler stops before the profile is applied.
NtGdiGetAppClipBox used intersect_rect(), which leaves max/min values in the rect when the
intersection is empty.

Windows (MEASURED, probe clipbox.exe round 52 on the owner's Windows box, 11-24): a child
window wholly below its parent gives GetClipBox ret=1 (NULLREGION) box=(0,0)-(0,0); a child
inside gives ret=2 (SIMPLEREGION) (0,0)-(100,100) and a half-covered one ret=2 (0,0)-(100,61).
Wine 227 gave NULLREGION (0,0)-(0,-1646) for the child below its parent; with this patch it
gives (0,0)-(0,0) like Windows, and the inside and half rows do not change.

Not covered: a mapped DC (non-identity window/viewport) or RTL layout with an empty clip also
gets (0,0)-(0,0) now; Windows behavior there is not measured.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-227cz = 227 + this win32u.so x2; unedited build == 227's win32u.so):
- 3440x1440, Camera Matching NT+IN, B&W 01+04: fix on 4/4 + 4/4 applied (two sessions);
  kill switch NEUTRON_CLIPBOX_EMPTY_ZERO=0 on the same build 0/4. 3840x2160 fix on: 2/2 applied.
- Sanity (fix on): Develop slider drag, filmstrip thumb click, Masking "Add New Mask" panel OK.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_CLIPBOX_EMPTY_ZERO=0.
--- a/dlls/win32u/clipping.c	2026-11-24 19:49:16.889400919 -0500
+++ b/dlls/win32u/clipping.c	2026-11-24 19:49:16.890400952 -0500
@@ -428,6 +428,20 @@
 }
 
 
+/* NEUTRON #59: on Windows a clip box that comes out empty (NULLREGION) is
+ * all zeros, like GetRgnBox of an empty region.  Wine left the leftover of
+ * the failed intersection with the device rect in it, e.g. (0,0)-(0,-26)
+ * for a child window that lies wholly below its toplevel's visible rect,
+ * and Lightroom's Profile Browser turned that inverted rect into an invalid
+ * range, which aborted the click (Neutron#59).
+ * Kill switch: NEUTRON_CLIPBOX_EMPTY_ZERO=0. */
+static BOOL neutron_clipbox_empty_zero(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (v < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_CLIPBOX_EMPTY_ZERO" ); v = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return v;
+}
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           NtGdiGetAppClipBox    (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -458,6 +472,8 @@
         rect->right = tmp - 1;
     }
     dp_to_lp( dc, (LPPOINT)rect, 2 );
+    if (ret == NULLREGION && neutron_clipbox_empty_zero())
+        rect->left = rect->top = rect->right = rect->bottom = 0;
     /* NEUTRON READ-TRACE */
     if (neutron_read_band_hit( rect ))
         ERR( "neutron-read: GetAppClipBox dc=%p hwnd=%p ret=%d box=(%d,%d)-(%d,%d)\n",
